  "correct": "3",
  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n(16 (2)/(5)-12 (1)/(15)) div 3 (4)/(81)= { ? } \n\nConcept used: \n\n [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/fc6adb90fa5c83ccc02b63de50366d728a9db8992e44c36c2388d3390f187850.png] \n\n \n\n**Calculation:**\n\nConvert (16 (2)/(5)) and (12 (1)/(15)) to improper fractions:\n\n⇒ 16 (2)/(5) = (82)/(5)\n\n⇒12 (1)/(15) = (181)/(15)\n\n⇒ (82)/(5) - (181)/(15) \n\n⇒ (82 times 3)/(5 times 3) - (181)/(15) = (246)/(15) - (181)/(15) = (65)/(15)\n\nSimplify (65)/(15) to (13)/(3)\n\n⇒ 3 (4)/(81) = (247)/(81)\n\n⇒ (13)/(3) div (247)/(81) = (13)/(3) times (81)/(247) = (13 times 81)/(3 times 247) = (27)/(19)\n\n \n\n**Therefore, the simplified result is 1 (8)/(19).**",
